{
  "title": { "en": "One-to-one" },
  "tray": "proof",
  "fact": "inject",
  "intro": [
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "Two values made by the same constructor are equal only if their arguments are: if S a = S b, then a = b. This is <wiki-ref to=\"injectivity\"></wiki-ref>. The declaration does not give it as a rule; it is proved with the help of a function, pred, the number before a number."
      }
    }
  ],
  "after": {
    "en": "The one-to-one proved goes into the “Rule book of numbers”. In Lean’s kernel the same fact is called noConfusion."
  },
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "in-inject_1",
      "kind": "define",
      "words": ["everyday", "terms"],
      "step": { "en": "The one before" },
      "fn": "pred",
      "on": 0,
      "rows": [
        { "lhs": "pred(zero)", "choices": ["zero", "s(zero)"] },
        { "lhs": "pred(s(x))", "choices": ["x", "s(x)", "pred(x)"] }
      ],
      "tests": [
        { "term": "pred(s(s(zero)))", "value": "s(zero)" },
        { "term": "pred(s(zero))", "value": "zero" },
        { "term": "pred(zero)", "value": "zero" }
      ],
      "solution": ["zero", "x"],
      "naive": ["zero", "pred(x)"],
      "brief": {
        "en": "Write a right side for every row."
      },
      "hint": [{ "en": "Nothing comes before 0, so take 0." }]
    },
    {
      "id": "in-inject_2",
      "kind": "proof",
      "step": { "en": "S is one-to-one" },
      "consts": ["zero"],
      "words": ["everyday", "terms"],
      "cases": [],
      "tests": [{ "premises": { "p": "∀x. pred(s(x)) = x" }, "goal": "∀x. ∀y. s(x) = s(y) → x = y" }],
      "brief": {
        "en": "From the definition of pred, prove: if S x = S y, then x = y."
      },
      "hint": [
        { "en": "Take a, and then b, in pred’s definition." },
        { "en": "The assumed S a = S b can rewrite one of them." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "gx = allI[x=a](body: gy) {",
        "  body {",
        "    gy = allI[x=b](body: f) {",
        "      body {",
        "        f = impI[A=\"s(a) = s(b)\"](body: w2) {",
        "          body {",
        "            e1 = allE[t=a](p)",
        "            e2 = allE[t=b](p)",
        "            w1 = rewrite[at=[0]](f.body, e1)",
        "            w2 = rewrite[at=[0]](w1, e2)",
        "          }",
        "        }",
        "      }",
        "    }",
        "  }",
        "}",
        "goal <- gx"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
